{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgKhjcHafw8jgsKgC8u0h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a fix to the tab bar icons, which still render as filled rounded squares on Home and Payment. The glyph vectors inherit a large filled rect from the icon component's 48x48 frame fill, so clearing the instance root fill is not enough. I clear fills on the non-vector containers inside each tab instance and keep the vectors only.\n\nTwo text overlaps show on Home: the \"New Arrivals\" sub at y=1390 sits against the title at y=1366 with height 22, ending at 1388, so I nudge the sub to y=1394. In the card master, Name sits at ph+10 with height 38 and Desc at ph+50 (170), so long names like \"IWC Schaffhausen 2021 Pilot's Watch\" collide with \"Luxury automatic chronograph.\" I restructure the master card: Name at ph+8, height 32, lh 15; Desc at ph+42, height 28, lh 13; Price at ph+74; Was/Off and Rating at ph+100. I apply this on the masters (17:145 grid, 17:160 deal), so all instances follow. Separately I read the reaction counts on children of the sign-in chain.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":1862,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":239309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1862}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55c7d231-d4f6-406f-a88f-ed2764d489e7","uuid":"752fd666-b24c-487f-a74a-33e7b713319d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:30:08.516Z","thinking_duration_ms":13685}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgKhjcHafw8jgsKgC8u0h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Private list of what still needs doing:\n\n1. **Tab-bar icons are still filled blocks** on Home and Payment. Clearing the instance root was not enough: each icon component carries an inner container frame that paints the same grey, so the block survives. I have to clear fills on every non-vector descendant inside each tab instance and keep only the glyph vectors.\n2. **Card text collides** on Home: long product names run into their description lines (\"IWC Schaffhausen 2021 Pilot's Watch\" over \"Luxury automatic chronograph\"), and the New Arrivals subtitle crowds its heading. That is a master-component spacing problem, so I fix it on the deal and grid card components rather than per instance.\n3. **Prototype coverage audit** — most links live on child nodes rather than frames, so I need to count reactions across the whole subtree of each screen to report coverage honestly.\n4. **Final report** — file URL, page ID, all 15 screen IDs, flow summary, limitations.\n\nThe fix write and the reaction audit read touch different things and neither needs the other's output, so both go in this response."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":1862,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":239309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1862}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55c7d231-d4f6-406f-a88f-ed2764d489e7","uuid":"c167c8ea-ba99-499f-912f-cc9969862d43","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:30:15.441Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgKhjcHafw8jgsKgC8u0h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YHXHVk4wtFdU86cB8iCZYq","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const page = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === '5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfor (const s of ['Regular','Medium','SemiBold','Bold']){ try{ await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Montserrat',style:s}); }catch(e){} }\nconst log=[];\nconst ACTIVE={r:0.9725,g:0.2157,b:0.3451};\nconst IDLE={r:0.4,g:0.439,b:0.522};\nconst frames=['17:188','17:417','17:673','17:898'].map(figma.getNodeById);\nconst succ=figma.getNodeById('17:956');\nconst behind=succ && succ.children.find(c=>c.name==='13_Payment (behind)');\nif(behind) frames.push(behind);\n\nframes.forEach(f=>{\n  if(!f) return;\n  const isPayment = /13_Payment/.test(f.name);\n  f.children.filter(c=>/^Nav · /.test(c.name)).forEach(inst=>{\n    const label=inst.name.replace('Nav · ','');\n    const active = isPayment ? label==='Cart' : label==='Home';\n    inst.fills=[];\n    inst.findAll(x=>{\n      if(x===inst) return;\n      if(x.type==='VECTOR'){ x.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:active?ACTIVE:IDLE}]; return; }\n      if(x.type==='FRAME' || x.type==='GROUP' || x.type==='COMPONENT' || x.type==='INSTANCE' || x.type==='RECTANGLE'){\n        // keep the tiny active dot, clear any painting container\n        if(x.name!=='Active dot') x.fills=[];\n      }\n    });\n    const dot=inst.findOne(x=>x.name==='Active dot');\n    if(dot) dot.fills = active? [{type:'SOLID',color:ACTIVE}] : [];\n    const lbl=inst.findOne(x=>x.type==='TEXT');\n    if(lbl) lbl.fills=[{type:'SOLID',color:active?ACTIVE:IDLE}];\n  });\n  log.push('nav fixed '+f.name);\n});\n\n// Card typography: rebuild text positions on both card masters\nfunction restyleCard(c){\n  const name=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Name');\n  const desc=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Desc');\n  const price=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Price');\n  const was=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Was');\n  const off=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Off');\n  const rating=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Rating');\n  const ph=c.findOne(x=>x.name==='Photo');\n  const phH=ph?ph.height:150;\n  if(name){ name.y=phH+8; name.resize(name.width,34); name.lineHeight={value:15,unit:'PIXELS'}; name.fontSize=12; }\n  if(desc){ desc.y=phH+44; desc.resize(desc.width,26); desc.lineHeight={value:12,unit:'PIXELS'}; desc.fontSize=9; }\n  if(price){ price.y=phH+72; }\n  if(was){ was.y=phH+74; }\n  if(off){ off.y=phH+88; }\n  if(rating){ rating.y=phH+94; }\n  const star=c.findOne(x=>x.type==='INSTANCE' && /Icon_Star/.test(x.name));\n  if(star) star.y=phH+96;\n  log.push('card restyled '+c.name);\n}\n['17:145','17:160','17:175'].forEach(id=>{const c=figma.getNodeById(id); if(c) restyleCard(c);});\n\n// New Arrivals subtitle spacing\nconst home=figma.getNodeById('17:188');\nconst na=home.children.find(c=>c.name==='New Arrivals');\nconst nas=home.children.find(c=>c.name==='New Arrivals sub');\nif(na&&nas){ nas.y=na.y+26; }\nconst dt=home.children.find(c=>c.name==='Deal title');\nconst tm=home.children.find(c=>c.name==='Deal timer');\nif(dt&&tm){ tm.y=dt.y+22; tm.resize(160,14); }\n\nreturn JSON.stringify({log:log});","description":"Clear tab icon blocks and fix card text spacing","fileKey":"t59Fpla3t3vTCJcBn4Rv7i"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":1862,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":239309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1862}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55c7d231-d4f6-406f-a88f-ed2764d489e7","uuid":"21df4341-ecea-4370-945e-939834d9bfff","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:30:20.414Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YHXHVk4wtFdU86cB8iCZYq","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgKhjcHafw8jgsKgC8u0h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01sOZVuC5aPpt6ZVNFhJ7bE9","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const page = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === '5:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nfunction countReactions(node){\n  let n=0;\n  (function walk(x){\n    if(!x) return;\n    try{ if(x.reactions && x.reactions.length) n+=x.reactions.length; }catch(e){}\n    if(x.children) x.children.forEach(walk);\n  })(node);\n  return n;\n}\nconst out=page.children.filter(c=>/^\\d\\d_/.test(c.name)).map(c=>({name:c.name,id:c.id,links:countReactions(c),hasReactions:false}));\nreturn JSON.stringify({screens:out, total: out.reduce((a,b)=>a+b.links,0)});","description":"Audit prototype reaction coverage per screen","fileKey":"t59Fpla3t3vTCJcBn4Rv7i"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":1862,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":239309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1862}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"55c7d231-d4f6-406f-a88f-ed2764d489e7","uuid":"dd8a3231-a946-4d48-a860-d6478210ba9f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T05:30:22.349Z","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01sOZVuC5aPpt6ZVNFhJ7bE9","display_name":"Use Figma","server_display_name":"figma-authenticated-proxy","tool_name":"use_figma"}]}
