e and page**\n\n- File: https://www.figma.com/design/t59Fpla3t3vTCJcBn4Rv7i/\n- Page: `03 · Workspace`, node `5:2`\n- Component library: section `10:2`, holding the reused platform shell plus my own button set, text-field states, header, bottom navigation, size chips, search bar, quantity stepper and the grid, deal, row and photo card components.\n\n**Screens**\n\n| # | Frame | Node |\n|---|---|---|\n| 01 | Splash | 14:28 |\n| 02 | Onboarding_Choose_Products | 14:43 |\n| 03 | Onboarding_Make_Payment | 14:68 |\n| 04 | Onboarding_Get_Your_Order | 14:95 |\n| 05 | Sign_In | 14:121 |\n| 06 | Sign_Up | 14:163 |\n| 07 | Forgot_Password | 14:211 |\n| 08 | Get_Started | 14:234 |\n| 09 | Home | 17:188 |\n| 10 | Product_List | 17:417 |\n| 11 | Product_Detail | 17:673 |\n| 12 | Shopping_Bag | 17:848 |\n| 13 | Payment | 17:898 |\n| 14 | Payment_Success_Overlay | 17:956 |\n| 15 | Profile | 17:1026 |\n\n**Prototype**\n\n52 click interactions are wired. Onboarding chains 01 → 02 → 03 → 04 with Prev, Next and Skip; Sign In links to Login, Forgot Password and Sign Up; forgot password returns to sign in; both auth paths reach Get Started then Home. Trending and deal \"View all\" lead to the product list, cards lead to the product detail, and detail leads to the bag and payment. Continue on payment opens the success overlay, which returns to Home. The tab bar navigates Home, Cart and Setting from every screen that carries it.\n\n**Limitations**\n\n- Figma rejects a NAVIGATE action whose destination is the frame that owns the trigger, so the Similar To cards on the product detail are static, and the current tab on its own screen is not a link.\n- The splash advance is a click rather than a timed auto-advance, because the plugin API has no reliable delay trigger.\n- Home, Product List, Product Detail and Profile are tall scrolling frames rather than 812-high clips, per the brief's allowance for vertical scroll.","ttft_ms":4369,"type":"result","duration_ms":2065128,"uuid":"ceb8856d-082a-4